From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Subject: [PATCH] WSC: retry with a fresh enrollee transaction

The bounded M1 retry still leaves an extender partially onboarded when an M2
is lost and a later key exchange is rejected.  A cold rev150 deployment showed
all three initial M1 frames, only two M2 frames at the agent, and the missing
radio retrying the same 499-byte M1.  The controller sent the first retry M2,
which was lost, then rejected the next two exchanges in
EVP_PKEY_derive_set_peer.  A final M1 was lost and the four-attempt budget was
exhausted.  The agent remained in wsc_m2_pending with no operational BSS.

An M1 retry is a new WSC transaction, so regenerate the enrollee nonce and DH
keypair before serializing it.  Patch 0023 already regenerates the registrar
half for every received M1; refreshing both halves prevents a rejected key
from being repeated.  Allow eight bounded retries (24 seconds at the existing
three-second interval), still well inside the controller command lifetime and
large enough to tolerate loss of both an M1 and its M2 during tri-band startup.

Repeated initialization exposed an upstream ownership leak: em_crypto_t::init
copies generated key material into m_crypto_info but never releases the DH or
EVP generation objects on success.  Release those temporary objects after the
copy so retries do not leak cryptographic state.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 src/em/config/em_configuration.cpp | 10 ++++++++--
 src/em/crypto/em_crypto.cpp         | 11 +++++++++++
 2 files changed, 19 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/em/config/em_configuration.cpp b/src/em/config/em_configuration.cpp
--- a/src/em/config/em_configuration.cpp
+++ b/src/em/config/em_configuration.cpp
@@ -6081,7 +6081,7 @@ void em_configuration_t::handle_state_wsc_m1_pending()
 // number of M1 re-sends used to solicit a fresh M2. Reset each time a fresh M1 is
 // sent (handle_autoconfig_resp).
 #define EM_AGENT_M2_RESEND_TICKS 3
-#define EM_AGENT_M2_MAX_RESENDS  4
+#define EM_AGENT_M2_MAX_RESENDS  8
 
 void em_configuration_t::handle_state_wsc_m2_pending()
 {
@@ -6102,6 +6102,15 @@ void em_configuration_t::handle_state_wsc_m2_pending()
         return;
     }
 
+    // A retry starts a new WSC transaction.  Refresh the enrollee nonce and
+    // DH keypair so an exchange rejected by OpenSSL is not repeated with the
+    // same enrollee material.  The controller independently refreshes its
+    // registrar half for every received M1.
+    if (m_crypto.init() != 0) {
+        em_printfout("radio %s failed to refresh WSC crypto before M1 retry",
+            util::mac_to_string(get_radio_interface_mac()).c_str());
+        return;
+    }
     unsigned char msg[MAX_EM_BUFF_SZ];
     int msg_len = create_autoconfig_wsc_m1_msg(msg, get_peer_mac());
     if (msg_len < 0) {
diff --git a/src/em/crypto/em_crypto.cpp b/src/em/crypto/em_crypto.cpp
--- a/src/em/crypto/em_crypto.cpp
+++ b/src/em/crypto/em_crypto.cpp
@@ -211,6 +211,18 @@ int em_crypto_t::init()
     m_crypto_info.r_pub_len = static_cast<unsigned int> (BN_num_bytes(pub_key));
     m_crypto_info.r_priv_len = static_cast<unsigned int> (BN_num_bytes(priv_key));
     
+    // The generated values have been copied into m_crypto_info; the OpenSSL
+    // objects are temporary.  init() is also used for WSC retransmissions, so
+    // retaining these on every successful call creates an unbounded leak.
+#if OPENSSL_VERSION_NUMBER < 0x30000000L
+    DH_free(dh); // owns p, g, pub_key and priv_key after DH_set0/generate
+#else
+    EVP_PKEY_free(param_pkey);
+    EVP_PKEY_CTX_free(pkey_ctx);
+    EVP_PKEY_free(pkey);
+    cleanup_bignums(p, g, priv_key, pub_key);
+#endif
+
     return 0;
 bail:
 
